rom 24.6% to 29.4%) and syphilis (from 5.0% to 12.5%).\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Trends in HIV prevalence and incidence were evaluated for statistical significance using chi-square and Poisson exact tests.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"HIV and syphilis incidence were computed among those who tested negative for HIV or syphilis at first visit, who returned for testing later.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Poisson exact test was used to evaluate trends in HIV and syphilis incidence; chi-square test for trend was used elsewhere.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}